{
  "id": "V007",
  "description": "Absence of a standing vote is a third state: an abandoned half-ballot must not read as rejection of the movies the voter never reached",
  "spec_clause": "Cross-cutting rules: 'Never conflate no with not yet seen ... an abandoned half-finished ballot silently reads as rejection of every movie the voter never reached, and the coverage rule stops working entirely.'",
  "rationale": "5 attendees. u4 and u5 abandoned their swipe stack after m1: they have rows for m1 but none for m2. m1: 5 rows, 4 yes -> coverage 5/5 = 1.00, approval 4/5 = 0.80, yes = 4. m2: 3 rows (u1,u2 yes; u3 no) -> attendee_votes 3, coverage 3/5 = 0.60 (exactly at floor, passes), approval 2/3 = 0.6667 >= 0.50, yes = 2. Both eligible, both clear the floor -> two finalists -> Phase 2 runs. If the missing rows were read as 'no', m2 would show attendee_votes 5, approval 2/5 = 0.40 < 0.50, be dropped from the finalists, and m1 would win outright with Phase 2 skipped - a different documented outcome. Runoff: m1 vs m2 = 3 (u1,u2,u3) to 2 (u4,u5) -> m1 beats m2, and beating every other finalist makes it the Condorcet winner.",
